    Btw, skimming review process from CONTRIBUTING.md, it may require one additional committer to be reviewed (have a right to bind voting). Do I understand right?&lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="15072515" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 28 Dec 2015 07:33:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user minahlee commented on the pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/574#issuecomment-167503210&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/574#issuecomment-167503210&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    @HeartSaVioR It&apos;s not mandatory to have review from PPMC/committer since we follow lazy consensus rule but always good to be reviewed by more people including non-committer.&lt;br/&gt;
    Check 5th bullet from &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;The Review Process&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#the-review-process&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#the-review-process&lt;/a&gt;) for the detail.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15072517" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 28 Dec 2015 07:35:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user Leemoonsoo commented on the pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/574#issuecomment-167503853&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/574#issuecomment-167503853&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    According to CONTRIBUTING.md, a committer review is required, not one additional committer. So technically, nothing stops push committer self reviewed code. However, in Zeppelin project, committers used to initiate lazy consensus (&quot;merge if there &apos;re no more discussions&quot;) instead of pushing self reviewed code directly, when there&apos;re no review from other committers.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15072520" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 28 Dec 2015 07:37:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user HeartSaVioR commented on the pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/574#issuecomment-167504561&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/574#issuecomment-167504561&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    @minahlee @Leemoonsoo &lt;br/&gt;
    Thanks for letting me know. Zeppelin&apos;s review process is a bit uncommon so I was confused. It&apos;s cleared.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15072524" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 28 Dec 2015 07:47:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user Leemoonsoo commented on the pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

